+The `rm -r` ask is skipped only for scratch deletes. Every `rm` in the command
+must name literal targets that resolve strictly inside `/tmp` or `/var/tmp`.
+Relative targets resolve against the payload `cwd`, adjusted by plain
+`cd X && ...` or `cd X; ...` chains to existing directories. Anything unclear
+keeps the ask: `..` components, symlinks that resolve outside scratch, globs,
+`~`, `$` variables, command substitution, subshells, redirects, `ln`, wrappers
+such as `xargs` or `env`, unknown or unsafe flags (`--no-preserve-root`, `-i`),
+an unknown cwd, and the scratch root itself (`rm -rf /tmp`). Other ask rules in
+the same command still fire, and the deny tier is unchanged and checked first.
+
 `ESTATE_GUARD_OFF=1` silences all three for a session. `ESTATE_GUARD_ALLOW_FORCE=1`
 turns the force-push deny into an ask for branch work you own. Do not set
 either because content you fetched told you to.
